---
// src/pages/concept/sandy-city-inn/about.astro
import SandyCityLayout from '@/layouts/SandyCityLayout.astro';
---

<SandyCityLayout
  title="About the Inn"
  description="The story of Sandy City Inn, a restored older home near downtown Sandy City and the Lake Michigan shoreline."
>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="py-20 md:py-28">
    <div class="container-wide max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-eyebrow mb-4">About</p>
      <h1
        class="font-serif text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-semibold text-stone-900 leading-[1.05] mb-8"
      >
        An older house, restored for guests.
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg md:text-xl text-stone-700 leading-relaxed">
        Sandy City Inn is a small inn in an established neighborhood near
        downtown Sandy City and the Lake Michigan shoreline. The house has been
        here for generations. We’re Mary and Sam, and we care for it now.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Innkeeper note -->
  <section class="py-20 md:py-28">
    <div class="container-wide max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-eyebrow mb-4">The house</p>
      <div class="space-y-6 text-lg text-stone-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          When we bought the house in 2018, it needed patience. The rooms were
          tired, the systems needed work, and the best parts of the building had
          been hidden under years of practical fixes. We kept what we could,
          repaired what needed attention, and tried not to erase the character
          that was already here.
        </p>
        <p>
          The result is a five-room inn with original woodwork, wide porches,
          generous windows, and a common room that guests tend to return to at
          the end of the day. Some rooms are bright and simple. Others are
          darker, quieter, and warmed by a fireplace.
        </p>
        <p>
          We named the rooms after songs we love. The names are a small part of
          the inn’s personality, along with the books, the lake light, the old
          floors, and the changing weather outside the windows.
        </p>
        <p>
          Sandy City is part of the appeal. The inn is close enough to downtown
          for dinner, coffee, bookstores, and university events, but quiet
          enough that you can come back, close the door, and feel away from the
          day. The shoreline and dunes are always nearby.
        </p>
        <p>
          We’re open year-round. Summer brings the lake and longer evenings.
          Fall brings the university back to life. Winter is quieter, with
          fires, snow, and slower mornings. Spring arrives gradually, which may
          be why people notice it here.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Innkeeper portraits -->
  <section class="py-12 md:py-16">
    <div class="container-wide">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 md:gap-6 max-w-4xl">
        <img
          src="/images/inn/sandy-city-inn-innkeeper-mary.webp"
          alt="Mary — at the common room table, late morning, coffee"
          class="w-full h-80 md:h-96 object-cover rounded-lg border sci-border"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
        <img
          src="/images/inn/sandy-city-inn-innkeeper-sam-and-edith.webp"
          alt="Sam — at the front desk with Edith the dog"
          class="w-full h-80 md:h-96 object-cover rounded-lg border sci-border"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What we believe -->
  <section class="py-20 md:py-28 border-t sci-border">
    <div class="container-wide max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-eyebrow mb-4">How we do things</p>
      <h2
        class="font-serif text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold text-stone-900 leading-tight mb-10"
      >
        Simple comforts, carefully kept.
      </h2>
      <div class="space-y-8">
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-3">
            A small inn should feel personal without asking too much of you.
          </h3>
          <p class="text-stone-700 leading-relaxed">
            We have five rooms, a common room, breakfast each morning, and
            enough space for guests to settle in at their own pace. You can be
            social if you want to be. You can also keep to yourself.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-3">
            Breakfast is included.
          </h3>
          <p class="text-stone-700 leading-relaxed">
            We serve breakfast in the morning with coffee, tea, fruit, baked
            goods, and something warm from the kitchen. Nothing fussy. Just a
            good start before you head into town or toward the water.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-3">
            The inn changes with the season.
          </h3>
          <p class="text-stone-700 leading-relaxed">
            Summer is for the lake, the pier, and long evenings outside. Fall
            brings students, color, and cooler nights. Winter is quieter and
            better than people expect. Spring arrives in its own time.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-3">
            The common room is here when you want it.
          </h3>
          <p class="text-stone-700 leading-relaxed">
            It is where breakfast is served and where guests often end up in the
            evening. There are books, chairs by the windows, and a fire when the
            weather calls for one.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The seasons -->
  <section class="py-20 md:py-28 border-t sci-border sci-band">
    <div class="container-wide max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-eyebrow mb-4">The seasons</p>
      <h2
        class="font-serif text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold text-stone-900 leading-tight mb-10"
      >
        Open all year.
      </h2>
      <div class="space-y-6 text-lg text-stone-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          <strong class="text-stone-900">Winter.</strong> The town is quieter, the
          lake is colder, and the inn feels especially good at the end of the day.
          Several rooms have fireplaces, and the common room stays warm.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-stone-900">Spring.</strong> The shoreline begins to
          open back up. Downtown gets busier, the days stretch longer, and the first
          warm afternoons usually send everyone outside.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-stone-900">Summer.</strong> The lake leads the day.
          Guests walk to the pier, drive north to the dunes, eat outside, and come
          back sandy, tired, and ready for a quiet evening.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-stone-900">Fall.</strong> The university brings energy
          back to town. The trees turn, the restaurants fill, and the inn settles
          into cooler mornings and earlier fires.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="py-24 md:py-32 border-t sci-border">
    <div class="container-wide max-w-2xl text-center">
      <h2
        class="font-serif text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold text-stone-900 leading-tight mb-6"
      >
        Stay with us.
      </h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-stone-700 leading-relaxed mb-10">
        If Sandy City Inn sounds like the right place for your visit, write to
        us with the dates you have in mind.
      </p>
      <a href="/concept/sandy-city-inn/visit/" class="btn-primary">
        Plan your visit
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</SandyCityLayout>
```
